{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty","id":1150317,"title":"Rick and Morty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-17T06:30:13-07:00","id":1150317,"title":"Rick and Morty","content":"I've recently been thinking about a game set in the Rick and Morty setting. Especially since seeing The Ricklantis Mixup a few weeks ago. It gave me the idea to center it around the Citadel of Ricks. So that all PCs can play their own version of Rick or Morty. And for a system I was thinking of Mage. I think it has everything this crazy setting needs. I'll just add the rule; no such thing as vulgar magic!<br /> As a bit of an experiment I already tried to write-up Rick as a Starting M:tA PC:<br /> <br /> Name: Rick Sanchez D10<br /> Tradition: Sons of Ether<br /> Essence: Dynamic<br /> Nature: Curmudgeon<br /> Demeanor: Rogue<br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1<br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 5, Appearance 1<br /> Mental: Perception 2, Intelligence 5, Wits 3<br /> Talents: Awareness 1, Dodge 1, Expression 1, Intimidation 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Crafts 1, Drive 1, Firearms 2, Performance 1, Survival 1, Technology 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics 1, Computer 2, Cosmology 3, Investigation 1, Medicine 2, Occult 1, Science 3<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 2, Avatar 4, Contacts 2, Resources 1, Wonder 5 (Portal Gun)<br /> Arete: 3<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Quintessence: 4<br /> Spheres: Forces 2, Life 3, Matter 2<br /> Resonance: Dynamic 1<br /> Merits/Flaws: Addiction, Aging<br /> <br /> This is obviously not tv-show Rick, but that's the Rickest Rick. He'd have most Spheres nearly maxed out, do a bit better with Abilities too. Instead this is a PC Rick, with still some room to grow. And every player would have their own take.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 10-17-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:33:46-07:00","id":1150363,"title":"","content":"Thoughts:<br /> <br /> Morty count as an &quot;ally&quot;, but I'm not sure of morty's sister, I think most Ricks don't travel with her (taking by the amount of morty in the Citadel of Ricks).<br /> <br /> Who are the Contacts? because the other two family members are more relatives/antagonists than contacts (they will cause trouble and won't provide useful information most of the time). I think that contacts shal be gained while your Rick starts medling with the universe, these will be the outlaws and bizarre folk that Rick often asociates with.<br /> <br /> Don't make starting Rick so much aged. If this Rick it's starting then he just got the portal gun. He doesn't even know how to actually make it. Give Rick a break.<br /> <br /> Ricks have enemies, that's why the Council of Ricks exist (heck, even the Council it's midly antagonistic). I think Primordial Mark would be mandatory to represent you're have features that mark you as enemy of certain forms of &quot;authority&quot; from different universes, that will recognize you as a treath just by being you (basically, you could be held acountable for numerous crimes commited by Ricks in several dimensions). Also Enemy comes as a likely flaw.<br /> <br /> You have a very potent but disfunctional &quot;Chantry&quot; as background, The Council of Ricks. Unless you are a rogue like THE Rick, which it's dangerous, you're (forced to be) part of the Council just by having the Portal Gun. This actualy does allow you to have certain amout of resources in spite of the hostile attitude of other ricks, like exchanging stuff with other ricks and get a place to hide against your mandatory enemies. It also may come with responsibilities, I doubt many ricks *choose* to do the police job (or do it for free).<br /> <br /> Rick may aproach or be aproached by the SoE, but probably will be a rogue not just in demeanour but also in affiliation. I don't see him as the type to publish in Paradigma or go to Traditionalist reunions.<br /> <br /> I would rather choose Prime, Spirit and Forces as Spheres. Spirit it's important because a good deal of any Ricks experience it's off world (you have the portal gun after all). Prime it's important to become the master gadgeteer that you're fated to be. Forces it's more optional, it does allow to get a potent ray gun (Ricks are often seen using ray guns) but it's not the only option to do that.<br /> I think that sphere spread &quot;to be a rick&quot; should be optional with the condition of being geared towards being a device crafter, ray guns, and travel trough other worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-17-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:58:49-07:00","id":1150368,"title":"","content":"Allies can stand for either family or certain aliens, Contacts is just aliens. And Aged is pretty mandatory, every Rick is 70. But like I said the thing is that every player is allowed their own take. Feel free to demonstrate your own, if you think you can fit your vision in a basic starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T11:56:12-07:00","id":1150405,"title":"","content":"At least give them 2 points for the physical stats. Most Ricks are pretty prone to fighting, despite their age. I really don't think they would be so weak. I get that ageing is a thing, but really, 1's across the board? In the same vein, give them a few more points in Brawl and Melee.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious why you chose to stop at Tech and Science 3.<br /> <br /> Anyway, about the universe. Are we saying that the Citadel is kind of like the Gernsback Continuum? A horizon realm tucked away in its own quiet quadrant of the solar system somewhere?<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you want to stay really loyal to the show, you could outright ban the Time sphere. Harmon has gone on record as saying there will never be a Time Travel episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T13:50:13-07:00","id":1150454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150405#post1150405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least give them 2 points for the physical stats. Most Ricks are pretty prone to fighting, despite their age. I really don't think they would be so weak. I get that ageing is a thing, but really, 1's across the board?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the Aging Flaw works. Take away one level of Physical stats for every decade the PC is over 40, Rick is about 70. And I don't think making his Social or Mental Attributes <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">tertiary</span></span> makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150405#post1150405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the same vein, give them a few more points in Brawl and Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what can go with less points to make that possible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150405#post1150405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious why you chose to stop at Tech and Science 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>In M:tA Revised you can't go over 3 on any Abilities with Freebies. I couldn't spare those Freebies. Besides there's no proof one way or the other Rick is especially good with 'real' tech or science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150405#post1150405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and if you want to stay really loyal to the show, you could outright ban the Time sphere. Harmon has gone on record as saying there will never be a Time Travel episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's much more to the Time Sphere than time travel. Like the way Rick stopped time at the end of the first season. Although it wasn't Rick doing it, there was actual time travel in the season 2 opener.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T16:26:39-07:00","id":1150496,"title":"","content":"All I can say is sticking to new character creation rules is severely limiting how rick these Ricks can possibly be.<br /> <br /> Is there really any need for it?<br /> <br /> Good call about the stop time thing though, I'd then rephrase it to banning time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T00:52:11-07:00","id":1150566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150496#post1150496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can say is sticking to new character creation rules is severely limiting how rick these Ricks can possibly be.<br /> <br /> Is there really any need for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not new at all, I used the basic Revised system. And I don't see the problem. Citadel Ricks are generally not all that impressive. It appears a lot of them don't even have a portal gun. And it's not like you get to play on the setting's highest powerlevel in any other RPG. PCs need a challenge and room to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:42:51-07:00","id":1150718,"title":"","content":"Well, you <i>could </i>use Masters of the Art creation rules fo a significantly more capable Rick, but it's true that most Ricks don't show high level stuff other than the portal gun (then again, we don't see a lot about them). It's also true that Ricks tend to solve everything with rayguns, or running, all of which would be impaired by low Physical.<br /> <br /> Now, Aging it's a Defect and thus, as all Defects, <i>it's an optional rule</i> (Merits/Defects are an optional rule, any ST can switch that option off if it doesn't serve a purpose, and nothing breaks). Having that in mind, I would allow not having that Defect if you want to play an aged character that has retained it's attributes (by doing exercise) You <i>did age</i>, but it's not a Defect because it didn't impaired your character (that's what a Defect is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-18-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T14:12:26-07:00","id":1150775,"title":"","content":"I just did a write-up for a Morty as well. The character creation rules actually got me pretty close to the main Morty we know:<br /> <br /> Name: Morty Smith M2000<br /> Tradition: Orphan<br /> Essence: Questing<br /> Nature: Conformist<br /> Demeanor: Child<br /> Physical: Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3<br /> Social: Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> Mental: Perception 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> Talents: Alertness 2, Awareness 2, Brawl 1, Dodge 1, Expression 1, Leadership 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> Skills: Crafts 2, Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Firearms 2, Melee 1, Performance 1, Stealth 2, Survival 2, Technology 1<br /> Knowledges: Computer 1, Cosmology 2, Enigmas 1, Investigation 1, Occult 1,<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 1, Arcane 1, Avatar 5,<br /> Arete: 3<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Quintessence: 5<br /> Spheres: Life 3, Mind 2, Spirit 2<br /> Resonance: Entropic 1<br /> Merits/Flaws: Aging<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150718#post1150718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you <i>could </i>use Masters of the Art creation rules fo a significantly more capable Rick,</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing what I could do with the basic character generation rules was the point of this experiment though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150718#post1150718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's true that most Ricks don't show high level stuff other than the portal gun (then again, we don't see a lot about them).</div> </div> </div> </div>And in The Ricklantis Mixup we even see a few Ricks that don't even have that, leaving them stuck on the Citadel. My thinking with the above Rick is that he has a portal gun, but not the ability to construct one himself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150718#post1150718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Aging it's a Defect and thus, as all Defects, <i>it's an optional rule</i> (Merits/Defects are an optional rule, any ST can switch that option off if it doesn't serve a purpose, and nothing breaks). Having that in mind, I would allow not having that Defect if you want to play an aged character that has retained it's attributes (by doing exercise) You <i>did age</i>, but it's not a Defect because it didn't impaired your character (that's what a Defect is).</div> </div> </div> </div>I needed to max out my Flaws. And since he's 70, Aging just seemed like the natural choice. It's not like his lifestyle is all that healthy either. The case could be he's using superscience to beef himself up physically when he needs to. And again; this is just a Rick. In a party of R&amp;Ms everyone can follow their own vision on the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 10-19-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:41:15-07:00","id":1150817,"title":"","content":"Would you like us to just say it's brilliant and requires no changes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T01:21:08-07:00","id":1150929,"title":"","content":"Would you like me to do this with your comments in this topic?<br /> <br /> But no, any kind of response is welcome. I'm just not served that well with the message that I have to ignore the basic M:tA character creation rules. Cause for me that was the entire point of the exercise. It's not about the perfect Rick C-137 write-up. Just seeing how close I can get with a limited amount of points. So I need to know where you'd get the points for any changes. Tell me where on the character sheet my Rick could actually spare a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T17:46:52-07:00","id":1151166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1150929#post1150929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you like me to do this with your comments in this topic?<br /> <br /> But no, any kind of response is welcome. I'm just not served that well with the message that I have to ignore the basic M:tA character creation rules. Cause for me that was the entire point of the exercise. It's not about the perfect Rick C-137 write-up. Just seeing how close I can get with a limited amount of points. So I need to know where you'd get the points for any changes. Tell me where on the character sheet my Rick could actually spare a few.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem stems around that Ricks aren't on the level of recently awakened mages. That's what the MtA character creation rules are designed to make, recently awakened mages. Rick's simply aren't at that level. they are more on the level of diciples, or on the cusp of mastery. C-137 Rick might be an Archmage, but the others have to be somewhere higher than a recently awakened one in order to still be Ricks.<br /> <br /> As an exercise, it's not bad, but what I think it illustrates is that the Rickiest Rick this creation system could make when rigidly following it by the letter is a pretty terrible Rick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:58:06-07:00","id":1151254,"title":"","content":"I think we've seen quite a few Citadel Ricks in the Ricklantis Mixup that are in fact weaker than a starting M:tA character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T06:52:35-07:00","id":1151295,"title":"","content":"Then all I can say is a character with so many 1s in so many different places is going to be a real pain to play, and will probably not make your players feel like Ricks. If that's what you want out of your game then so be it. I honestly think you're letting rules get in the way of a making a character.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry, but Average Ricks and Average Mortys having the same ar\u00eate is just silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T22:42:34-07:00","id":1151583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1150317-rick-and-morty?p=1151254#post1151254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we've seen quite a few Citadel Ricks in the Ricklantis Mixup that are in fact weaker than a starting M:tA character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd make the argument there are quite afew Sleeper Ricks in The citadel. Actually I'd argue they probably have roughly similar base stats with Arete being their levels of &quot;protagonism&quot; Most Ricks are sleepers. Those who go on adventures are Awake. Rick c-137 is probably an arch-mage.<br /> <br /> Either way I'd swap Aging as a flaw for multiple derangements. That should give you a healthy dose of extra points to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 10-21-2017, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T07:24:39-07:00","id":1152189,"title":"","content":"Average Mortys should be sleeper acolites. They all should be able to use some of Rick technology because anyone can use Devices with the right mindset and &quot;training&quot;...and if our average Rick can't or won't make Devices, well, his technology isn't user friendly enough for the average Morty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:53:57-07:00","id":1202398,"title":"","content":"Going to the Rickest-Rick that can be made with the basic creation rules, I'd go with the Enhancements background, since Rick is literally a cyborg. Dimensional Science and Forces are a must. Derangement: Depression and Megalomania. Addiction flaw. Appearance and Charisma 1, Manipulation 4. Strength 2, Dexterity 4, Stamina 2. His mental traits are so outrageous that it is impossible to do them justice with the standard rules, so I'll just go Percep 3, Int 4, Wits 3. Yeah, that's a decent Rick. It's not the RIckest Rick by any means, but it would be recognizably close while still being allowable in a beginner game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}